Hello all,

I just completed my third ascension and am moving steadily down the
list in alphabetical order.  It took me 3 tries to ascend this
character.  But after the 2 YASD's I played more carefully and managed
to pull it off.

I decided that this time I would play genoless and polyless.
Fortunately I did not step on any poly traps, and I restrained myself
from using my unicorn horn for dipping.  Genoless was not actually
that hard as I did use Elbereth to protect myself from L and h.  Green
slimes were darted and/or avoided.

There were 3 graveyard levels in the main dungeon and wraith luring
and letting my pet dragon kill them brought me from Level 12 to 30
without having to use any potions of gain level.  I think I gained 20
or so levels from wraiths.

I had also intended to go wishless but I have insufficient patience to
deal with the consequences of my failed tengu reverse-genociding
experiment:  I set up with my pet dragon in the first level of Sokoban
and reverse genocided tengu.  After the dragon killed each one I would
tin it and then eat the tin collections.  Acquiring teleportitis was
easy enough, but after going through two magic markers and recharging
them I wished for a ring of teleport control.   Then once I had broken
wishless I figured what the heck since I was having very little luck
enchanting my weapons and armor.  Blessed?oEA and EW were giving me +1
gains and I used additional wishes on magic markers.

I wore a robe for most of the game and used that to cast identify and
that made the midgame much easier.  Unfortunately I let a nymph borrow
the robe near the end of the game and I could not find her.  No big
loss but no more identify after that point.

I had a hard time deciding on the best missile weapon and melee
weapon.  For missile weapons I went with darts for operator ease.  I
could have used a bow and thereby gotten d2 shots per turn but with
the weapon-exchanging and all of that I just enchanted up a stack of
darts, poisoned them, blessed them, and called it done.  I did not
have much use for missile weapons in any case as my melee was strong
and evasion was easy too.

I alternated between Frostbrand and the Sceptre of Might.  I avoided
Mojo because the damage did not seem to compare as well and I hate to
destroy wands.  Being Neutral, most of the monsters I encountered were
either Lawful or Chaotic.  For neutral monstes (minotaurs, being one)
I would switch to Frosty if I could be bothered, spend more turns in
melee, or just walk on past.  If possible I would avoid using
Frostbrand so as to preserve potions.
I analyzed Mojo, Frosty, Sceptre of Might, and a silver saber and came
up with the following average damages given best case scenarios (e.g.
non-aligned, undead or demon, not cold resistant, not shock-resistant,
etc.).
