I did make use of an amulet of lifesaving.  This was nearly a YASD as
I was making liberal use of a cockatrice corpse when I decided to cast
identify.  Well, I forgot to put my gauntlets of power back on before
weilding the rubber chicken.  Whew!

I started the ascension run by hitting the Wizard with a cockatrice
corpse.  Unfortunately I had forgotten force bolt and did not have a
wand of striking.  I had to go down a couple of levels to find a
recently slain ElvenKing and use his pickaxe to bust up the statue.
With the Book of the Dead finally firmly in hand I took the express
elevator down to the VS, did the dance, and took the elevator down to
the yard.  I did not have a wand of secret door detection but the Bell
of Opening and a scroll of charging did the trick.  After killing the
high priest, I uncursed my stack of teleport scrolls and c!oGL back
up.

Then it was:
50 - 49 - 48 - 47 - 46 - 45 - 44 potion up - 43 potion up - 42 potion
up - 41 black glow - 40 - 39 ..
38 the Wizard returns, and immediately drinks a cursed potion of gain
level!
37 wack Wizard with cockatrice corpse ( I would kill new ones whenever
I saw one and bless it, they kept very fresh that way).
Double check inventory for amulet theft ... oops, I know I put it here
someplace ... wait maybe the Wizard stole it without me paying
attention ... oops I must have left it downstairs!!!  So, I recursed
my teleport scrolls and made a return visit to the sanctum.  I felt
quite silly.

Endgame was uneventful with 400+ hp, free action, conflict, 19
teleport zaps available and 14 wand of death zaps.  I even had some
poly zaps but I was worried about hitting an object and losing my
conduct.

